Peios packaging helpers
=======================

Build-time tools shared by Peios package recipes. They are not commands for
people: recipes call them by path.

/usr/libexec/peios-packaging/split-debug [options] PACKAGE PATH...

    Splits debug information out of every ELF file and static archive under
    PATH. Each ELF's DWARF source paths are rewritten to
    /usr/src/debug/PACKAGE, dwz removes its duplicate DWARF (per file; an ELF
    over dwz's DIE limit is kept unoptimised), its debug sections go to a
    build-ID-indexed file
    under usr/lib/debug/.build-id, and the file is stripped; archives lose only
    their debug sections. The sources the DWARF references are copied to
    usr/src/debug/PACKAGE. It fails rather than skipping an ELF with no build
    ID or no debug information (--allow-stripped accepts a prebuilt blob).
    Options: --stage DIR, --build-root DIR.

/usr/libexec/peios-packaging/collect-rust-licences --licence-root DIR --root CRATE... [options]

    Run in a vendored Cargo workspace. For the root crates' normal and build
    dependency closure it copies each crate's LICENSE, COPYING and NOTICE files
    to DIR/<crate>-<version>/, writes DIR/crate-licenses.tsv, and prints the
    SPDX expression the shipped binaries are under. --check FILE fails unless
    that TOML file's [package].license equals it. --notice PREFIX=FILE supplies
    a reviewed notice for git crates that carry none of their own.
